'''Cyclone Stages''' are a group of time-limited stages that introduce the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, a set of enemies with non-stop attacks and extremely high health and attack power.

Once encountered, Cyclones will be recorded in the [[Enemy Guide]]. If the stage is completed, there is a chance to get a unique, new [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] or [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]] anti-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] Cat (30-40% drop rate). Units unlocked from Cyclone Stages usually also have their own [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]], which share the same schedule with the stages from which the cats are unlocked.

Cyclones have a general trait of being reasonably slow (with the exception of [[Primeval Cyclone]] and [[Dark Cyclone]]) and having low attack range (with the exception of [[The Perfect Cyclone]]), however they also often sport high health and damage along with a constant attack rate, meaning they can push with extreme ease. [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Control]] ([[:Category:Cats with Freeze ability|freeze]], [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|slow]] and [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|knockback]]) units are therefore essential against them to limit their destruction.

